    "qualification": "Separate CI runner instance and CPU model. PR12 did not expose a progressive first-page milestone. Current completion includes one early edit and cooperative loading pauses. These observations are not a controlled speedup ratio."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "Single native process run per revision; automated input frame intervals include driver scheduling.",
    "A screenshot is evidence of the rendered result, not a comparison against the Figma original.",
    "Harness waits do not change the app worker/runtime deadlines.",
    "Gesture samples are warmed by a completed native save/settle before sampling; page-entry timing is recorded separately.",
    "Reopen measures document open in a fresh process after app launch, not cold-disk or app-start latency; startup library listing may already have read/warmed storage or overlap the open.",
    "Progressive import/reopen completion includes one early page-name edit and the app cooperative pauses for that interaction. First-editable and first-paint marks precede that edit.",
    "First paint is the runtime milestone after two animation frames following editable mount (with a one-second fallback), not a measurement of all bitmap/font decoding or complete visual settling.",
    "Early edit latency measures change to the observed Stored indicator; a subsequent host snapshot independently verifies ACK and page name. It is not exact fsync duration.",
    "The entire source archive/shared graph is decoded before first-page publication. A very large first page still carries its complete conversion cost.",
    "Cached reopen is conditional on a fresh, bounded, self-contained first-page cache. Missing, stale, oversized or unsuitable caches use full open; older documents obtain a cache on a later successful save.",
    "Full Yjs restoration and large-page publication still perform synchronous main-process work. A visible early edit can wait seconds for a durable acknowledgment.",
    "Full source import still takes tens of seconds; progressive availability does not remove total conversion, validation and checkpoint work.",
    "Software rendering on a two-core CI runner; frame intervals are not hardware GPU FPS.",
    "Working-set snapshots are not a combined process peak or a decoded-image cache budget. Asset garbage collection and a decoded-pixel memory ceiling are not implemented.",
    "Drag and the measured post-load page rename still have material end-to-end latency. Individual observations do not prove all editing or pan workloads are smooth.",
    "Known conversion losses include effects, variable bindings, component semantics, masks, mixed text and font availability. Import fidelity remains unverified.",
    "This run does not qualify full-fixture four-peer native collaboration or current packaged macOS/Windows builds."
  ],
